     {"id": "AI-CONIC-MIXED-THIRD-JET-002", "title": "A universal rational three-jet family on the mixed cubic conic component", "origin": "Owner-directed Codex continuation", "status": "proof-written-unreviewed", "evidence": "research/ai/2026-10-23-conic-third-jets/proof.md", "statement": "For every complex a,b,d with d nonzero and c=-d^3, PR101's specified first jet with normal class[1:d] extends through order three in rank-twelve incidence of two fourteen-row maps of the canonical112-cubed source after changing its second coefficient. Exported maps belong to Q[a,b,d,d^-1], with pole order at most two. Independent literal-source replay checks all19600 moving-kernel coefficients in each positive order and constant leading minor determinants1,1,-1. A five-field second correction and explicit third matrices are supplied; the third matrices have52 and48 nonzeros, with16 source-correction coefficients.", "dependencies": ["PR101 cubic-component base and first jet, credited and pinned", "Explicit rational coefficient matrices and source-kernel corrections", "Independent literal4096-term source contraction and rational-function identities", "Unit leading-minor identities and coefficient specialization in Q[a,b,d,d^-1]"], "limitations": "The d=0 cubic fiber is outside the theorem. Does not assert that every first representative extends, a fourth-order extension, an all-order lift, the full matrix target, or a smaller exponent. No independent mathematical review, formalization or historical priority.", "independent_review": false, "lean_formalized": false, "improves_omega": false},
     {"origin": "Owner-directed OpenAI Codex continuation", "status": "proof-written-unreviewed", "evidence": "research/ai/2026-10-23-regular-unit-image/proof.md", "independent_review": false, "lean_formalized": false, "improves_omega": false, "id": "AI-PARTIAL-UNIT-REGULARITY-001", "title": "All-order Laurent regularity from a partial regular unit image", "section": "1-4", "statement": "Let a source slice space A in Mat_N have minimum nonzero first-slice and row-contraction ranks mu_A,mu_B. Let an injective D-dimensional target slice space in Mat_R have a unit and minimum rank nu. In a complete formal degeneration with one regular full-rank column map C and regular unit lift S, suppose rank(S(0)C(0))>=r. Put e=R-r and q=N-r. If mu_A>3q, nu-2e>q and D>dim(A)-mu_B+q, then both other maps are regular and the limit is an ordinary restriction. Independent source frames and e+1 target left inverses recover the complete long map. Every finite Laurent pole order is allowed.", "dependencies": ["Prior normalized Laurent rank lemma in AI-CYCLIC-REGULAR-UNIT-003", "Elementary rank loss under two-sided compression and independent regular frame completion", "Finite varying-left-inverse recovery identity"], "limitations": "The three strict inequalities, a regular full-rank long map and a regular target-unit lift are required. Written unreviewed proof; finite controls do not formalize arbitrary series. No general degeneration exclusion or exponent improvement."},
     {"origin": "Owner-directed OpenAI Codex continuation", "status": "proof-written-unreviewed", "evidence": "research/ai/2026-10-23-regular-unit-image/proof.md", "independent_review": false, "lean_formalized": false, "improves_omega": false, "id": "AI-A4-UNIT-IMAGE-EXCLUSION-002", "title": "A4 Laurent exclusion for regular unit images of rank at least109", "section": "5", "statement": "There is no A4 to M(10,10,11) complex formal degeneration if one long map C is regular with rank110 limit, the source lift of the target identity is regular, and rank(S(0)C(0))>=109. In particular source unit slices of corank at most one are included. At r109 the strict margins are7,6,1; Laurent regularity reduces to the prior ordinary rank contradiction12>11. The assertion is symmetric in the two long legs and covers every finite pole order.", "dependencies": ["AI-PARTIAL-UNIT-REGULARITY-001", "Prior all-size cyclic source minimum rank a^2 and ordinary A4 exclusion"], "limitations": "Rank108 unit images, singular long-leg limits and polar unit lifts remain outside this result. No constructed target, independent review, formalization, historical priority or exponent improvement."},
-    {"id": "AI-RESOLVENT-SHARP-MINRANK-001", "title": "Sharp minimum matrix rank six for the fixed-resolvent limit space", "status": "proof-written-unreviewed", "origin": "Owner-directed OpenAI Codex continuation", "independent_review": false, "lean_formalized": false, "improves_omega": false, "evidence": "research/ai/2026-10-23-resolvent-minrank/proof.md", "section": "1-4", "statement": "Over every field, the explicitly defined fixed-resolvent limiting matrix space W has dimension 112 and minimum nonzero matrix rank exactly six. Its difficult 31-dimensional outer block admits 31 successive triangular six-by-six minor identities with unit diagonal factors and unit substitutions. Every two-sided compression with total rank-loss budget at most five is injective on W. If the 110-by-112 and 112-by-110 compression factors both have rank 109 and kill a nonzero X in W, then rank X = 6, ker X is contained in im C, X(im C) = ker P, im C = X^-1(ker P), and ker P lies in the final 28-dimensional source layer.", "dependencies": ["Maintained literal cyclic convolution source and unimodular source unit, pinned in sources.json", "PR103 fixed resolvent and high/low limiting-space definition at 96f3b513acb1bc92a235dd9041ceae18b0fd4c83", "Exact integer thirty-one-minor certificate and elementary matrix rank inequalities"], "limitations": "Ordinary matrix rank, not tensor slice rank. No classification of all rank-six matrices, arbitrary singular degeneration, independent review, formalization, or smaller exponent. The narrow target application is superseded by the concurrent regular-long-leg theorem."}
